{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Then Moses sang.</b> It is the usage of Holy Scripture to put the future tense in place of the past with the word אז: אז יבנה שלמה (1 Kings 11:7), אז ידבר יהושע (Joshua 10:12), אז יבדיל משה (Deuteronomy 4:41), and likewise in the language of Ishmael. Moses alone composed the song and taught it to Israel, and each one would sing, saying אשירה לה'. Similar to it: ויצו משה וזקני ישראל (Deuteronomy 27:1), for the commandment Moses alone stated, and the elders of Israel stated it to all." "<b>And they said, saying.</b> Each and every one thus, or in each and every generation." "<b>For He is highly exalted.</b> He showed His exaltedness, for the horse, which has pride and might, and the rider, who is mighty — both of them He cast into the sea like one shooting an arrow, for רמה בים is like נושקי רומי קשת (Psalms 78:9)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:38.025019484Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}